<LM_OUTPUT> {"role": "model", "feedback": "- Preprocess: fix feature selection. Your temporary overwrite of gene_index.json makes prior_genes == all genes, so n_genes stays ~25k. Remove the tmp gene_index write and build feature_genes from: HVGs ∪ curated-set genes (nonzero rows of existing geneset_membership) ∪ marker genes. Then subset adata to this set before reconcile_and_save_priors.\n- Cache graph tensors. In train_model(), precompute i_idx, j_idx, w once on device and pass to compute_graph_laplacian_penalty to avoid per-batch tensor construction overhead.\n- True input gene dropout. Apply 10% feature masking to x before enc_fc1 during training (e.g., with a Bernoulli mask) instead of/alongside encoder dropout.\n- Monitor a cleaner validation objective. Use val_core = NB_NLL + beta*(KL_z+KL_u) for ReduceLROnPlateau and early stopping; keep regularizers in the optimized loss but exclude them from the monitored metric.\n- Regularize residual latent. Add a small L1/L2 penalty on u_mu (e.g., ||u_mu||_1 with lambda_u=1e-4) to prevent W_res/u from absorbing pathway signal.\n- Save decoder params per spec. After training, export decoder_params.npz with bias, theta, and W_res, plus a reference to W_path; also save latents.npz with z_set_mu, u_resid_mu, and concatenated latents.\n- Memory/perf for W_path. Keep W_path sparse and use torch.sparse.mm, or at minimum cast W_path to float16 under autocast on CUDA to cut memory and speed matmul.\n- DataLoader perf. Use num_workers>0 and pin_memory=True for train/val/all loaders.\n- Exclusivity mask: restrict to sets with nonzero overlap to any marker cell type (drop rows/cols with group=-1) to reduce O(n_sets^2) cost.\n- Diagnostics: log z_set sparsity (fraction |z_mu|>τ) per epoch to track alignment; optionally try RESIDUAL_DIM=32 if prior coverage remains high to nudge interpretability without hurting ARI."} </LM_OUTPUT>

