Here is the feedback we got for generated code for model_training.py in the conversation:

<FEEDBACK>- Standardize/weight latents before kNN. Compute per-dimension mean/std on train (or all) for [z_set | u_resid] and z-score latents before neighbors. Additionally grid-search a residual scale α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1.0} (apply u_resid *= α) jointly with resolution (and K ∈ {10,15,20}) and pick by validation silhouette. This prevents high-variance dims (often u_resid) from dominating and reliably boosts ARI.
- Normalize W_path columns. L2-normalize geneset columns (and/or learn a per-set scalar) so TF-IDF-heavy sets don’t overwhelm others. This balances z_set contributions, yielding cleaner clusters.
- Avoid densifying W_path. Keep W_path as torch.sparse (or at least float16 under autocast) and use sparse matmul in decode. The saved memory/throughput allows larger batches or longer training, improving fit/ARI.
- True input gene dropout. Apply 10% Bernoulli masking on input X before enc_fc1 during training (separate from hidden dropout). This denoises and encourages reliance on stable pathway structure, improving cluster separation.
- Constrain residual pathway usage. Add a small penalty on u_resid activity (e.g., λ_u * mean(|u_mu|), λ_u≈1e-4) and optionally a column-wise group-lasso on W_res to prevent u/W_res from absorbing pathway signal. This increases z_set signal-to-noise and improves ARI.
- Bias initialization. Initialize decoder bias b to log(mean(counts)/1e4) per gene (or softplus^-1 of that mean) so μ starts near baselines. Faster convergence often lands in better minima with sharper clusters.
- Monitor the right metric. For LR scheduling/early stop, monitor a “core ELBO” (NB_NLL + β*(KL_z+KL_u)) on val; keep regularizers in the optimized loss but exclude them from the monitored metric. This reduces the risk of over-regularization driving selection away from best clustering.
- Gene-weight normalization. Normalize gene_weights to mean 1.0 (or sum n_genes) before applying in NB loss to keep the loss scale stable across runs; stabilizes training and downstream clustering.
- Exclusivity mask efficiency/quality. Build the exclusivity mask only for sets with nonzero marker overlap and precompute it once on device. Optionally weight mask entries by exclusivity strength (e.g., Jaccard of marker overlap) to better decorrelate conflicting marker-driven dims and sharpen clusters.
- Graph Laplacian speed. Precompute i_idx/j_idx/w tensors on device once and pass to the penalty each step to cut overhead; this allows more epochs within the same wall-clock.
- DataLoader perf. Set num_workers>0 and pin_memory=True for all loaders to increase throughput; combine with mixed precision on CUDA to fit larger batches.
- Reproducible Leiden and broader search. Set random_state for leiden and expand resolution grid (e.g., add 0.2, 1.6) to avoid missing better partitions; select by val silhouette as you do.</FEEDBACK>

